{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"936ac7541000db4f9937d8d733cb19c5ace817ec9d77ac25d857825b88329351","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM framework / Bedrock provider","key_entities":["build_bedrock_provider","resolve_bedrock_region","src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py","src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py","provenance_for","boto3.session.Session","REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION","AWS_DEFAULT_REGION","AWS_REGION","region_source","provider_provenance","tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py","tests/unit/test_verdict_provenance.py"],"problem_keywords":["region resolution","AWS_REGION","bedrock provider","environment variable","configuration precedence"],"propositions":["Rebar's Bedrock provider ignores AWS_REGION environment variable and fails to resolve region when only AWS_REGION is set, though this is the standard region variable modern AWS tooling uses","Botocore does not consult AWS_REGION during region resolution, so rebar must implement explicit region resolution before passing to boto3.Session to close this gap","A pure resolver function chain must establish precedence: REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION (config) > AWS_DEFAULT_REGION > AWS_REGION > boto3 ambient profile resolution, with both region and region_source recorded in provenance when bedrock provider is used","Error messages and docs currently document AWS_REGION as non-functional rather than fixing the provider to support it; these must be updated to reflect the corrected behavior and resolution chain"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787717238205491001,"uuid":"c8b3a2df-d723-4b7a-bc21-08e212e47ee3"}